-- This program is here to be refused, and `test/CliSmoke.lean` requires that it
-- be refused identically by `agent-cat plan`, `agent-cat cost` and `agent-cat
-- run`. It interpolates a flag into a prompt: a flag has no canonical text —
-- a language that silently picked "yes" would be a language whose prompts are
-- not determined by their source — so the checker rejects it rather than
-- choosing one. (Text splices as itself; a verdict as its objections.)
workflow {
  ok : flag <- ask person "owner"
    "Shall we?"

  note : text <- ask model "scribe"
    "Write this up: {ok}"
}
